#: lib/retro_hex_chat_web/controllers/help_content/feature_space_construct.html.heex:113
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Press F next to a chair or an armchair to sit down."
msgstr "Press F next to a chair or an armchair to sit down."

#: lib/retro_hex_chat_web/controllers/help_content/feature_space_construct.html.heex:44
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Stand next to one of these pieces and press E, or the hand button on a touch screen."
msgstr "Stand next to one of these pieces and press E, or the hand button on a touch screen."

#: lib/retro_hex_chat_web/controllers/help_content/feature_space_construct.html.heex:112
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "The Construct is kept just as it was left."
msgstr "The Construct is kept just as it was left."

#: lib/retro_hex_chat_web/controllers/help_content/feature_space_construct.html.heex:37
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Walls and corners turn like any other piece. A door in a wall lets people through."
msgstr "Walls and corners turn like any other piece. A door in a wall lets people through."

#: lib/retro_hex_chat_web/controllers/help_content/feature_space_construct.html.heex:102
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "In the %{floor} tab, pick a floor, then press and drag: the whole rectangle is painted. %{erase} makes it white again. You can walk on a painted floor and put pieces on it."
msgstr "In the %{floor} tab, pick a floor, then press and drag: the whole rectangle is painted. %{erase} makes it white again. You can walk on a painted floor and put pieces on it."

#: lib/retro_hex_chat_web/controllers/help_content/feature_space_construct.html.heex:81
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Lists the games, and each one opens in a new tab."
msgstr "Lists the games, and each one opens in a new tab."

#: lib/retro_hex_chat_web/controllers/help_content/feature_space_construct.html.heex:69
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Press E on one teleporter to arrive at the other one of its pair."
msgstr "Press E on one teleporter to arrive at the other one of its pair."

#: lib/retro_hex_chat_web/controllers/help_content/feature_space_construct.html.heex:57
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Press E to open the door, and again to close it. It stays open while someone is in the doorway."
msgstr "Press E to open the door, and again to close it. It stays open while someone is in the doorway."

#: lib/retro_hex_chat_web/controllers/help_content/feature_space_construct.html.heex:63
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Press E. The result appears on the piece and in the chat."
msgstr "Press E. The result appears on the piece and in the chat."

#: lib/retro_hex_chat_web/controllers/help_content/feature_space_construct.html.heex:75
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Shows a short text above it. Whoever put it up can change it, and the moderators can too."
msgstr "Shows a short text above it. Whoever put it up can change it, and the moderators can too."

#: lib/retro_hex_chat_web/controllers/help_content/feature_space_construct.html.heex:87
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Shows the channel's topic and the messages of its %{pinned} list. Only a channel's Construct has one."
msgstr "Shows the channel's topic and the messages of its %{pinned} list. Only a channel's Construct has one."

#: lib/retro_hex_chat_web/controllers/help_content/feature_space_construct.html.heex:94
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Shows the last picture posted in the conversation."
msgstr "Shows the last picture posted in the conversation."

#: lib/retro_hex_chat_web/controllers/help_content/feature_space_construct.html.heex:51
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Switches its light on or off."
msgstr "Switches its light on or off."

#: lib/retro_hex_chat_web/controllers/help_content/feature_space_construct.html.heex:25
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Some pieces, like a sofa or a long table, take up more floor than a chair. Turning one turns all of it, and only where it fits."
msgstr "Some pieces, like a sofa or a long table, take up more floor than a chair. Turning one turns all of it, and only where it fits."

#: lib/retro_hex_chat_web/controllers/help_content/feature_space_construct.html.heex:21
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "The palette in the top-left corner keeps the pieces in tabs, one for each theme and one for the End of Time. Choose one and click the floor to place it. It stays in your hand, so a row of chairs is a row of clicks. A see-through copy shows where it would go: green where it fits, red where it does not. Esc, or choosing it again, puts it away."
msgstr "The palette in the top-left corner keeps the pieces in tabs, one for each theme and one for the End of Time. Choose one and click the floor to place it. It stays in your hand, so a row of chairs is a row of clicks. A see-through copy shows where it would go: green where it fits, red where it does not. Esc, or choosing it again, puts it away."
